WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.319 --> 00:00:08.098
I’ll show you how to turn your story into a usable customer list. We use fictional example data.

2
00:00:08.136 --> 00:00:16.078
Start with a short description of your offer and target audience. BelgoBase turns that story into a concrete proposal you can review.

3
00:00:16.111 --> 00:00:23.200
You can add an existing customer list as context. This helps BelgoBase understand which kinds of companies already fit your business.

4
00:00:23.247 --> 00:00:29.084
Click Analyze list. Review what BelgoBase learns from your existing customer list.

5
00:00:29.124 --> 00:00:35.442
Next, review the proposed target audience. Check the description before running the search.

6
00:00:35.486 --> 00:00:44.001
Find these companies displays the selection. You can see location, revenue, profit, employees and source year in the same workspace.

7
00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:49.104
Select the companies you want to use next. Here we choose three examples.

8
00:00:49.147 --> 00:00:56.281
Choose Complete contact details and use the current search selection. BelgoBase then creates a clearly bounded contact task.

9
00:00:56.315 --> 00:01:01.737
Review the estimate and spending limit. If everything is correct, start the contact search.

10
00:01:02.173 --> 00:01:10.582
After the check, you can see which contact details were found and which row still needs review. Then export the verified contacts.

11
00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:17.729
Only confirm receipt after the download has completed. This lets BelgoBase keep the correct processing status.

12
00:01:17.773 --> 00:01:25.611
Your list is now in Excel, ready for further work. In BelgoBase, you can save the selection or refine it further.

bridge-0
